Arabic is a world language. About 400 million
people speak Arabic in the countries of the Middle
East and North Africa. Many millions more around
the world understand some Arabic because it is the
language of the Holy Qur’an.
The number of speakers of a world language is
always changing because the world is changing.
The number of Arabic speakers is rising every
year. But the number of Russian speakers is
falling. English is like Arabic: the number is rising.
More and more people are communicating in English
every day. Why? Because people from different
countries often speak English when they meet.
Palestinian leaders speak English when they meet to
talk about our country. It is the language of science
and technology – the language scientists, doctors,
businessmen and artists use.
About two billion people speak English in countries like
Britain, the United States, Australia and India. Many
more are learning it in schools all over the world.
